From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Gmeiner <cgmeiner@igalia.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Mar 2026 12:37:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 28/57] panvk: Wire clip prolog into draw path

When a draw uses shader clip distance, get the clip distance FS prolog
from the device's linked shader cache. It is compiled once per clip
distance count, against the VS's varying layout so its LD_VAR_BUF byte
offsets for CLIP_DIST0/1 match what the main FS reads, and keeps the
registers any FS may preload. It ends with a jump to the address in the
FAU word reserved for it. For each main FS, cache an SPD descriptor
pointing at the prolog.

Draws without a fragment shader still have to clip, so bind a
standalone prolog in that case. It keeps its own ATEST to commit the
coverage result, and the tiler must run the varying shader, which is
normally skipped without a fragment shader. Rasterizer discard skips
the standalone prolog.

Set skip_atest on the linked prolog so it does not emit a second ATEST
alongside the main FS's. Account for the prolog's discard in
shader_modifies_coverage, allow_forward_pixel_to_kill, early-Z /
late-Z update fields and the v13+ HSR fields.

Signed-off-by: Christian Gmeiner <cgmeiner@igalia.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/40343>
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c | 231 +++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 223 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

